  "id": "separation-anxiety",
  "term": "separation anxiety",
  "definition": "Separation anxiety can be a normal part of development in children around ages 1 to 3, but in its disorder form it may persist in children, adolescents, and some adults and can worsen over time. Early separation anxiety has also been described as a general vulnerability linked to later anxiety problems in adulthood.",
